  "description": "Pause (SPEC section 12), with the roster and prekeys of prekey.json. bob's loop breaker paused alice, so his reviewer session sends writer@alice a `pause` with every field, whose `reply_to` names the message it held, and later a `pause` saying the person lifted it; each is sealed to alice's prekey, and alice opens it at its `now` to `plaintext`. Neither carries text. Each `invalid_plaintexts` entry MUST be refused by the plaintext schema (reason `plaintext_malformed` when it arrives sealed). `older_kinds` are the kinds a client before `pause` knows: a plaintext schema of only those kinds MUST refuse both plaintexts, which is how an older client drops them (`plaintext_malformed`).",
